+### Angular Version
+- Angular 21.2 with the `@angular/build` builders; the app is zoneless by default (no `provideZoneChangeDetection`, no `zone.js` dependency). Evidence: `package.json`, `src/app/app.config.ts`.
+
+### Architecture
+- Components are standalone and list their own `imports`; there are no NgModules. Evidence: `src/app/app.ts`.
+- Angular classes inject dependencies with `inject()`, not constructor parameters. Evidence: `src/app/checkout.page.ts`.
+- A page is `src/app/<name>.page.ts` exporting `<Name>Page`, registered in `app.routes.ts`; top-level pages also get a link in `app.ts`. Evidence: `src/app/help.page.ts`.
+- All existing routes load eagerly with `component:` (observed; no lazy-loading decision is recorded). Evidence: `src/app/app.routes.ts`.
+- Services and stores are concrete `providedIn: 'root'` classes with no abstraction or token. Evidence: `src/app/order.service.ts`.
+
+### Component Design
+- New components set `changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`; the existing components do not yet (DEBT-006). Evidence: `src/app/products.page.ts`.
+- Templates are inline and use built-in control flow (`@if`, `@for` with `track`). Evidence: `src/app/cart.page.ts`.
+- Template-facing component members are `protected`, and `readonly` for fields. Evidence: `src/app/products.page.ts`.
+- Component selectors are `app-` kebab-case elements and directive selectors `app` camelCase attributes, enforced by lint. Evidence: `eslint.config.js`.
+
+### Forms
+- Forms are reactive and typed through `FormBuilder.nonNullable`, with field validators declared beside each control. Evidence: `src/app/checkout.page.ts`.
+
+### State Management
+- Shared state is a signal store: a private writable signal, a read-only view, `computed()` derivations and immutable updates. Evidence: `src/app/cart.store.ts`.
+- Component-only UI state is a signal on the component. Evidence: `src/app/checkout.page.ts`.
+
+### RxJS
+- RxJS appears only at the HTTP boundary; the one-shot order request is subscribed in the page with `next` and `error` handlers. Evidence: `src/app/checkout.page.ts`.
+
+### API / HTTP
+- One service per backend resource calls relative `/api/...` URLs with typed responses. Evidence: `src/app/order.service.ts`.
+- HTTP uses `provideHttpClient()` with no interceptors; request errors are handled by the calling component. Evidence: `src/app/app.config.ts`.
+
+### Typing
+- TypeScript `strict` and `strictTemplates` are on; data shapes are interfaces. Evidence: `tsconfig.json`.
+
+### Styling
+- Global styles live in `src/styles.css`; components declare no styles of their own. Evidence: `angular.json`.
+
+### SSR / Hydration
+- No SSR or hydration is configured. Evidence: `angular.json`.
+
+### Testing
+- Unit and component specs run on Vitest (globals, jsdom) through `@angular/build:unit-test`, beside the source as `*.spec.ts`. Evidence: `angular.json`, `tsconfig.spec.json`.
+- Component specs render the real template with `TestBed`, await `fixture.whenStable()` and assert on the DOM or store state. Evidence: `src/app/checkout.page.spec.ts`.
+- HTTP specs use `provideHttpClient()` with `provideHttpClientTesting()`. Evidence: `src/app/order.service.spec.ts`.
+- Test names are plain behaviour sentences. Evidence: `src/app/cart.store.spec.ts`.
+- Playwright specs import `test` from `e2e/fixtures.ts`, drive page objects from `e2e/pages/` and locate by role, label or text. Evidence: `e2e/place-order.spec.ts`.
+- Lint covers `src/**` only, so `e2e/` and `api/` are unlinted. Evidence: `angular.json`.
+- Target shape: trophy — `TestBed` component specs at the centre, few store and service specs, a thin Playwright layer for critical journeys.
