+---
+name: cart-state-in-memory
+description: CartStore holds cart items only in an in-memory signal, and e2e page objects reach the cart and checkout through in-app links
+type: gotcha
+scope: src/app/cart.store.ts, e2e/**
+status: verified
+last-verified: 2026-11-26
+---
+`CartStore` keeps items in a private signal that starts empty, and no code in `src/` writes them to browser storage or sends them to a server before checkout. `ShopPage.openCart` and `ShopPage.startCheckout` click links; the one `page.goto` in `ShopPage` opens `/`. The inference that a full page load empties the cart has not been executed.
+**Confidence:** observed
+**Provenance:** requested discovery draft from `/bootstrap`; `src/app/cart.store.ts`, `e2e/pages/shop.page.ts`
+**Evidence:** `CartStore.state` in `src/app/cart.store.ts`; `ShopPage` in `e2e/pages/shop.page.ts`
+**Counterevidence / exceptions:** none found; a search of `src/` for localStorage, sessionStorage, indexedDB and document.cookie had no match
+**Dependencies / unresolved:** whether losing the cart on reload is intended
+**Verify by:** reread `src/app/cart.store.ts` and repeat the storage search
+**Semantic refresh:** trigger: a change to `src/app/cart.store.ts` or added persistence; result: source reread and storage search on 2026-11-26.
+**Draft status:** draft pending PR review; not team-approved policy
