+---
+name: local-order-api-process
+description: npm start serves the app with an /api proxy to port 4301, and the order API is a separate Node process
+type: context
+scope: package.json, proxy.conf.json, playwright.config.ts, api/**
+status: verified
+last-verified: 2026-11-26
+---
+The `start` script runs `ng serve --proxy-config proxy.conf.json`, which forwards `/api` to `http://localhost:4301`. It does not start `api/server.mjs`, and no manifest script does. `node api/server.mjs` is the command `playwright.config.ts` uses for it, alongside the app on port 4300. Outside CI, Playwright reuses servers already running on the configured URLs.
+**Confidence:** observed
+**Provenance:** requested discovery draft from `/bootstrap`; `package.json`, `proxy.conf.json`, `playwright.config.ts`
+**Evidence:** `scripts.start` in `package.json`; `webServer` in `playwright.config.ts`
+**Counterevidence / exceptions:** `npm run e2e` starts both processes itself
+**Dependencies / unresolved:** how production runs the API is not visible in this repository
+**Verify by:** reread the `start` script and the `webServer` setting
